§ `Schedule 2 to the Order -- paragraph 1 of Part I of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations (personal allowances)`

-- Each head is tried in the order the Schedule gives it; "(a) ... except where head (b) or (c) of this sub-paragraph
-- applies" is written out, so the order of the arms does not change the answer.

§§ `Schedule 2 (1) -- single claimant`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 paras 1A and 11(1)(a): whether either is met is an input.
-- src:188 | (3) In Part I of Schedule 2 (applicable amounts: personal allowances)—
-- src:189 | (a) the sums specified in paragraph 1 shall be as set out in Schedule 2 to this Order; and
@ref art 20(3)(a) (src:188-189)
-- src:521 | Schedule 2 — PARAGRAPH 1 OF PART I OF SCHEDULE 2 TO THE INCOME SUPPORT REGULATIONS AS AMENDED BY THIS ORDER
-- src:522 | Part I — PERSONAL ALLOWANCES
-- src:523 | | (1) Person or Couple | (2) Amount |
-- src:524 | | (1) Single claimant aged— | (1) |
-- src:525 | | | (a) | except where head (b) or (c) of this sub-paragraph applies, less than 18; | | (a) | £75.65; |
-- src:526 | | | (b) | less than 18 who falls within any of the circumstances specified in paragraph 1A; | | (b) | £75.65; |
-- src:527 | | | (c) | less than 18 who satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a); | | (c) | £75.65; |
-- src:528 | | | (d) | not less than 18 but less than 25; | | (d) | £75.65; |
-- src:529 | | | (e) | not less than 25. | | (e) | £95.55. |
@ref Sch 2 (1) (src:521-529)
GIVEN `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 2 (1): the personal allowance of a single claimant` `the claimant's age` `the claimant falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND `the claimant falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A`
        THEN JUST 75.65   -- (b)
        IF `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)`
        THEN JUST 75.65   -- (c)
        IF `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND (NOT `the claimant falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A`) AND (NOT `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)`)
        THEN JUST 75.65   -- (a) except where head (b) or (c) applies
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18 AND `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 25
        THEN JUST 75.65   -- (d)
        IF `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 25
        THEN JUST 95.55   -- (e)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

