§§ `Schedule 2 (3) -- couple`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 reg 4ZA and Sch 2 para 1A; Jobseekers Act 1995 ss 3(1)(f)(iii) and 16; income-related employment and support allowance: whether each applies is an input.
-- "the claimant" is the person asking; "his partner" is the other member of the couple. Head (e) speaks of "the other
-- member" who is under 18, which can be either of them, so the facts about each are asked: whether each qualifies
-- (or would, were they not a couple) for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related ESA, satisfies
-- section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995, or is the subject of a section 16 direction. A case none of the
-- heads reaches (for example a claimant under 18 with a partner of 18 or over, where the claimant meets none of
-- (e)(i) to (iii)) is NOTHING.
-- src:535 | | (3) Couple— | (3) |
-- src:536 | | | (a) | where both members are aged less than 18 and— | | (a) | £114.35; |
-- src:537 | | | | (i) | at least one of them is treated as responsible for a child; or | | | |
-- src:538 | | | | (ii) | had they not been members of a couple, each would have qualified for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance; or | | | |
-- src:539 | | | | (iii) | the claimant’s partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (prescribed circumstances for persons aged 16 but less than 18); or | | | |
-- src:540 | | | | (iv) | there is in force in respect of the claimant’s partner a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (persons under 18: severe hardship); | | | |
-- src:541 | | | (b) | where both members are aged less than 18 and head (a) does not apply but one member of the couple falls within any of the circumstances specified in paragraph 1A; | | (b) | £75.65; |
-- src:542 | | | (c) | where both members are aged less than 18 and heads (a) and (b) do not apply; | | (c) | £75.65; |
-- src:543 | | | (d) | where both members are aged not less than 18; | | (d) | £150.15; |
-- src:544 | | | (e) | where one member is aged not less than 18 and the other member is a person under 18 who— | | (e) | £150.15; |
-- src:545 | | | | (i) | qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or who would so qualify if he were not a member of a couple; or | | | |
-- src:546 | | | | (ii) | satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (prescribed circumstances for persons aged 16 but less than 18); or | | | |
-- src:547 | | | | (iii) | is the subject of a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (persons under 18: severe hardship); | | | |
-- src:548 | | | (f) | where the claimant is aged not less than 18 but less than 25 and his partner is a person under 18 who— | | (f) | £75.65; |
-- src:549 | | | | (i) | would not qualify for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance if he were not a member of a couple; and | | | |
-- src:550 | | | | (ii) | does not satisfy the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (prescribed circumstances for persons aged 16 but less than 18); and | | | |
-- src:551 | | | | (iii) | is not the subject of a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (persons under 18: severe hardship); | | | |
-- src:552 | | | (g) | where the claimant is aged not less than 25 and his partner is a person under 18 who— | | (g) | £95.55. |
-- src:553 | | | | (i) | would not qualify for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance if he were not a member of a couple; and | | | |
-- src:554 | | | | (ii) | does not satisfy the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (prescribed circumstances for persons aged 16 but less than 18); and | | | |
-- src:555 | | | | (iii) | is not the subject of a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (persons under 18: severe hardship). | | | |
@ref Sch 2 (3) (src:535-555)
GIVEN `the claimant's age` IS A NUMBER
      `the claimant's partner's age` IS A NUMBER
      `at least one of them is treated as responsible for a child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one member of the couple falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 2 (3): the personal allowance of a couple` `the claimant's age` `the claimant's partner's age` `at least one of them is treated as responsible for a child` `the claimant qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple` `the partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple` `the claimant satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` `the partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995` `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the claimant` `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the partner` `one member of the couple falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `head (a)` THEN JUST 114.35
        IF `head (b)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (c)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (d)` THEN JUST 150.15
        IF `head (e)` THEN JUST 150.15
        IF `head (f)` THEN JUST 75.65
        IF `head (g)` THEN JUST 95.55
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `both members are aged less than 18` MEANS `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18 AND `the claimant's partner's age` LESS THAN 18
        `head (a)` MEANS
                `both members are aged less than 18`
            AND (       `at least one of them is treated as responsible for a child`
                  OR   (`the claimant qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple` AND `the partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple`)
                  OR    `the partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
                  OR    `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the partner`)
        `head (b)` MEANS
                `both members are aged less than 18`
            AND (NOT `head (a)`)
            AND `one member of the couple falls within a circumstance specified in paragraph 1A`
        `head (c)` MEANS
                `both members are aged less than 18`
            AND (NOT `head (a)`)
            AND (NOT `head (b)`)
        `head (d)` MEANS `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18 AND `the claimant's partner's age` AT LEAST 18
        `head (e)` MEANS
                (   `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18
                AND `the claimant's partner's age` LESS THAN 18
                AND (   `the partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple`
                     OR `the partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
                     OR `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the partner`))
            OR  (   `the claimant's partner's age` AT LEAST 18
                AND `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 18
                AND (   `the claimant qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple`
                     OR `the claimant satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
                     OR `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the claimant`))
        `the partner under 18 meets none of (i), (ii) and (iii)` MEANS
                `the claimant's partner's age` LESS THAN 18
            AND (NOT `the partner qualifies for income support under regulation 4ZA or income-related employment and support allowance, or would if not a member of a couple`)
            AND (NOT `the partner satisfies the requirements of section 3(1)(f)(iii) of the Jobseekers Act 1995`)
            AND (NOT `a direction under section 16 of the Jobseekers Act 1995 is in force in respect of the partner`)
        `head (f)` MEANS
                `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 18
            AND `the claimant's age` LESS THAN 25
            AND `the partner under 18 meets none of (i), (ii) and (iii)`
        `head (g)` MEANS
                `the claimant's age` AT LEAST 25
            AND `the partner under 18 meets none of (i), (ii) and (iii)`

§ `Schedule 3 to the Order -- Part IV of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations (weekly amounts of premiums)`

-- The row labels "15.—(2)" and so on are sub-paragraph numbers of paragraph 15, as the text prints them. Each
-- premium is for persons to whom a paragraph of the Regulations applies; whether it does is the Regulations'
-- (outside the text), so it is an input, and a person to whom it does not apply gets NOTHING (not covered).

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 paras 9, 9A and 10: whether the paragraph applies is an input.
-- src:194 | (5) The sums specified in Part IV of Schedule 2 (applicable amounts: weekly amounts of premiums) shall be as set out in Schedule 3 to this Order.
@ref art 20(5) (src:194)
-- src:556 | Schedule 3 — PART IV OF SCHEDULE 2 TO THE INCOME SUPPORT REGULATIONS AS AMENDED BY THIS ORDER
-- src:557 | Part IV — WEEKLY AMOUNTS OF PREMIUMS SPECIFIED IN PART III
-- src:558 | | (1) Premium | (2) Amount |
-- src:559 | | 15.—(2) Pensioner premium for persons to whom paragraph 9 applies. | (2) | £213.10. |
-- src:560 | | (2A) Pensioner premium for persons to whom paragraph 9A applies. | (2A) | £213.10. |
-- src:561 | | (3) Higher pensioner premium for persons to whom paragraph 10 applies. | (3) | £213.10. |
@ref Sch 3 (2), (2A), (3) (src:556-561)
GIVEN `paragraph 9 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 3 (2): the pensioner premium for persons to whom paragraph 9 applies` `paragraph 9 applies to the claimant` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 9 applies to the claimant` THEN JUST 213.10 ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 paras 9, 9A and 10: whether the paragraph applies is an input.
@ref Sch 3 (2A) (src:560)
GIVEN `paragraph 9A applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 3 (2A): the pensioner premium for persons to whom paragraph 9A applies` `paragraph 9A applies to the claimant` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 9A applies to the claimant` THEN JUST 213.10 ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 paras 9, 9A and 10: whether the paragraph applies is an input.
@ref Sch 3 (3) (src:561)
GIVEN `paragraph 10 applies to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 3 (3): the higher pensioner premium for persons to whom paragraph 10 applies` `paragraph 10 applies to the claimant` MEANS
    IF `paragraph 10 applies to the claimant` THEN JUST 213.10 ELSE NOTHING

-- src:562 | | (4) Disability Premium— | (4) |
-- src:563 | | | (a) | where the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a); | | (a) | £44.85; |
-- src:564 | | | (b) | where the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(b). | | (b) | £64.00. |
@ref Sch 3 (4) (src:562-564)
DECLARE `a condition of paragraph 11(1) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)`
    `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(b)`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 11(1): which condition is met is an input.
@ref Sch 3 (4) (src:562-564)
GIVEN `which condition` IS A `a condition of paragraph 11(1) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 (4): the disability premium` `which condition` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which condition`
    WHEN `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(a)` THEN 44.85   -- (a)
    WHEN `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 11(1)(b)` THEN 64.00   -- (b)

-- src:565 | | (5) Severe Disability Premium— | (5) |
-- src:566 | | | (a) | where the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(2)(a); | | (a) | £86.05; |
-- src:567 | | | (b) | where the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(2)(b)— | | (b) | |
-- src:568 | | | | (i) | if there is someone in receipt of a carer’s allowance or carer support payment or if he or any partner satisfies that condition only by virtue of paragraph 13(3A); | | (i) | £86.05; |
-- src:569 | | | | (ii) | if no-one is in receipt of such an allowance or payment. | | (ii) | £172.10. |
@ref Sch 3 (5) (src:565-569)
DECLARE `a condition of paragraph 13(2) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(2)(a)`
    `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(2)(b)`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 13(2) and (3A): which condition is met, and whether a carer is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, are inputs.
-- (5)(b)(i): "if there is someone in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment or if he or any partner
-- satisfies that condition only by virtue of paragraph 13(3A)"; (ii): "if no-one is in receipt of such an allowance
-- or payment".
@ref Sch 3 (5) (src:565-569)
GIVEN `which condition` IS A `a condition of paragraph 13(2) of Schedule 2 to the Income Support Regulations`
      `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 13(3A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 (5): the severe disability premium` `which condition` `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 13(3A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which condition`
    WHEN `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(2)(a)` THEN 86.05   -- (a)
    WHEN `the claimant satisfies the condition in paragraph 13(2)(b)` THEN
        IF `someone is in receipt of a carer's allowance or carer support payment, or the claimant or a partner satisfies the condition only by virtue of paragraph 13(3A)`
        THEN 86.05    -- (b)(i)
        ELSE 172.10   -- (b)(ii)

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 14: the number of children and young persons for whom the condition is satisfied is an input.
-- src:570 | | (6) Disabled Child Premium. | (6) £84.46 in respect of each child or young person in respect of whom the condition specified in paragraph 14 is satisfied. |
@ref Sch 3 (6) (src:570)
GIVEN `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the condition in paragraph 14 is satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 (6): the disabled child premium` `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the condition in paragraph 14 is satisfied` MEANS
    84.46 TIMES `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the condition in paragraph 14 is satisfied`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 14ZA: the number of persons who satisfy the condition is an input.
-- src:571 | | (7) Carer Premium. | (7) £48.15 in respect of each person who satisfied the condition specified in paragraph 14ZA. |
@ref Sch 3 (7) (src:571)
GIVEN `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 14ZA` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 (7): the carer premium` `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 14ZA` MEANS
    48.15 TIMES `the number of persons who satisfy the condition in paragraph 14ZA`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 13A: whether the conditions are satisfied, and whether the person is a child or in a couple, are inputs.
-- (8): three rows, each "in respect of" its own persons; the Order does not say that the rows are added, so each is
-- its own rule (fork F-09).
-- src:572 | | (8) Enhanced disability premium where the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied. | (8) |
-- src:573 | | | | | | (a) | £33.99 in respect of each child or young person in respect of whom the conditions specified in paragraph 13A are satisfied; |
@ref Sch 3 (8)(a) (src:572-573)
GIVEN `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 3 (8)(a): the enhanced disability premium for children and young persons` `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied` MEANS
    33.99 TIMES `the number of children and young persons in respect of whom the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied`

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 13A: whether the conditions are satisfied, and whether the person is a child or in a couple, are inputs.
-- src:572 | | (8) Enhanced disability premium where the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied. | (8) |
-- src:574 | | | | | | (b) | £22.00 in respect of each person who is neither— |
-- src:575 | | | | | | | (i) | a child or young person; nor |
-- src:576 | | | | | | | (ii) | a member of a couple or a polygamous marriage, |
-- src:577 | | | | | | | in respect of whom the conditions specified in paragraph 13A are satisfied; |
@ref Sch 3 (8)(b) (src:572-577)
GIVEN `the person is neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 3 (8)(b): the enhanced disability premium for a person who is neither a child or young person nor in a couple` `the person is neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is neither a child or young person nor a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` AND `the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of the person`
    THEN JUST 22.00
    ELSE NOTHING

-- out of text: Income Support Regulations 1987 Sch 2 para 13A: whether the conditions are satisfied, and whether the person is a child or in a couple, are inputs.
-- src:572 | | (8) Enhanced disability premium where the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied. | (8) |
-- src:578 | | | | | | (c) | £31.40 where the claimant is a member of a couple or a polygamous marriage and the conditions specified in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage. |
@ref Sch 3 (8)(c) (src:572-578)
GIVEN `the claimant is a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 3 (8)(c): the enhanced disability premium for a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the claimant is a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` `the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a member of a couple or polygamous marriage` AND `the conditions in paragraph 13A are satisfied in respect of a member of that couple or polygamous marriage`
    THEN JUST 31.40
    ELSE NOTHING
